From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:34:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: power: supply: apple,tristar-charger: Add the
 D2207

The iPad Air 2 charges through the same Tristar port controller, with a
D2207 PMIC instead of a D2365. The D2207 has the same charger functions
at other register addresses, so its compatible names the PMIC:
apple,d2207-tristar-charger, with apple,j81-tristar-charger for the
board.

The source events become optional: the iPad Air 2 subscribes none (see
its device tree), and the charger's poll of the connection state notices
a change without them.

Assisted-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../power/supply/apple,tristar-charger.yaml   | 23 ++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/apple,tristar-charger.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/apple,tristar-charger.yaml
index c8556e9c3..8e4acf9f7 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/apple,tristar-charger.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/apple,tristar-charger.yaml
@@ -11,7 +11,9 @@ maintainers:
 
 description: |
   Charging on Apple devices whose Lightning port uses a Tristar (NXP CBTL1610)
-  port controller and a D2365-family PMIC, such as the iPad 5 and iPad 6. The
+  port controller and a D2365-family PMIC, such as the iPad 5 and iPad 6 (D2365)
+  and the iPad Air 2 (D2207). The PMICs have the same charger functions at
+  different register addresses, so the compatible names the PMIC. The
   node is a child of the PMIC. It identifies the attached source through the
   Tristar and the PMIC ADC and sets the PMIC input-current limit, which iBoot
   leaves at 100 mA. PMU events come from the PMIC's event interrupt
@@ -27,11 +29,15 @@ allOf:
 
 properties:
   compatible:
-    items:
-      - enum:
-          - apple,j71b-tristar-charger
-          - apple,j71t-tristar-charger
-      - const: apple,tristar-charger
+    oneOf:
+      - items:
+          - enum:
+              - apple,j71b-tristar-charger
+              - apple,j71t-tristar-charger
+          - const: apple,tristar-charger
+      - items:
+          - const: apple,j81-tristar-charger
+          - const: apple,d2207-tristar-charger
 
   reg:
     items:
@@ -46,7 +52,7 @@ properties:
       - const: adc
 
   interrupts:
-    minItems: 3
+    minItems: 2
     maxItems: 16
     description: |
       From the PMIC's event interrupt controller. The first is the PMU event
@@ -54,7 +60,8 @@ properties:
       withdraws a grant there, before it knows which event it was. The
       second is ADC conversion complete. Every further entry is an event
       that can signal a change of the attached source (attach, detach,
-      charger state); any of them starts a new identification.
+      charger state); any of them starts a new identification. Without
+      them, the charger's poll of the connection state notices a change.
 
   apple,tristar:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
